IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`

-- Magna Carta (1215), English translation in McKechnie 1905: CHAPTERS 9 TO 11.
-- Debt: seizure of a debtor's land or rent (9), sureties (9), interest on a deceased
-- borrower's debt to the Jews (10), and the widow, the minor children and the payment of
-- the debt out of the residue (11).
-- Terms the text does not define, taken as plain facts: debt, chattels, surety, indemnified,
-- the Jews (as the text's name for a class of lenders), dower, necessaries, the holding of the
-- deceased, feudal lords' service (see NOTES.md, "Terms the text does not define").
-- Where the text names no one who bears a duty (9.2, 10.1, 11) the rule is a decision function
-- and not a regulative rule (forks F9, F10, F11).
-- GENERATED from tools/templates/mc15-ch09-11.l4.in by tools/build.py; edit the template.

§ `Chapters 9 to 11 -- debts and sureties`

§§ `Chapter 9 -- seizure for debt`

-- "Neither we nor our bailiffs": the King and a bailiff are the two parties the text names.
-- For any other officer the text does not say, and the answer is `Bar not covered`.
-- src:25 | Neither we nor our bailiffs shall seize any land or rent for any debt, so long as the chattels of the debtor are sufficient to repay the debt;
@ref Chapter 9 clause 9.1 (src:25)
GIVEN officer IS A Party
      `the chattels of the debtor are sufficient to repay the debt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 9 -- land or rent may be seized for the debt` IS
    IF   officer EQUALS `the King`
      OR officer EQUALS `a bailiff`
    THEN IF `the chattels of the debtor are sufficient to repay the debt`
         THEN Barred
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so long as the chattels of the debtor are sufficient to repay the debt".
         ELSE `Not barred`
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: so long as because "so long as" conditions the chattels being sufficient; the branch is reached by an officer other than the King or a bailiff, whom the sentence does not name).
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

-- src:25 | Neither we nor our bailiffs shall seize any land or rent for any debt, so long as the chattels of the debtor are sufficient to repay the debt;
@ref Chapter 9 clause 9.1 (src:25)
GIVEN officer IS A Party
      `the chattels of the debtor are sufficient to repay the debt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 9 -- neither the King nor his bailiffs shall seize land or rent for a debt while the chattels suffice` IS
    IF `ch 9 -- land or rent may be seized for the debt` officer `the chattels of the debtor are sufficient to repay the debt` EQUALS Barred
    THEN PARTY officer
         SHANT `seize land or rent for a debt`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY officer BECAUSE "ch 9: land or rent was seized for a debt while the chattels of the debtor sufficed to repay it"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The text does not say who may distrain the sureties (passive "shall ... be distrained"): fork F9.
-- src:25 | nor shall the sureties of the debtor be distrained so long as the principal debtor is able to satisfy the debt;
@ref Chapter 9 clause 9.2 (src:25)
GIVEN `the principal debtor is able to satisfy the debt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 9 -- the sureties of the debtor may be distrained` IS
    IF `the principal debtor is able to satisfy the debt`
    THEN Barred
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so long as the principal debtor is able to satisfy the debt".
    ELSE `Not barred`

-- src:25 | nor shall the sureties of the debtor be distrained so long as the principal debtor is able to satisfy the debt;
-- src:25 | and if the principal debtor shall fail to pay the debt, having nothing wherewith to pay it, then the sureties shall answer for the debt;
@ref Chapter 9 clause 9.2-9.3 (src:25)
GIVEN `the principal debtor is able to satisfy the debt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal debtor has failed to pay the debt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `ch 9 -- the sureties answer for the debt` IS
    IF `the principal debtor is able to satisfy the debt`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "so long as the principal debtor is able to satisfy the debt" and "if the principal debtor shall fail to pay the debt, having nothing wherewith to pay it".
    THEN `Not obliged`
    ELSE IF `the principal debtor has failed to pay the debt`
         THEN Obliged
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and if the principal debtor shall fail to pay the debt, having nothing wherewith to pay it".
         ELSE `Not obliged`

-- src:25 | and if the principal debtor shall fail to pay the debt, having nothing wherewith to pay it, then the sureties shall answer for the debt;
@ref Chapter 9 clause 9.3 (src:25)
GIVEN `the principal debtor is able to satisfy the debt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal debtor has failed to pay the debt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 9 -- the sureties shall answer for the debt if the principal debtor fails and has nothing wherewith to pay` IS
    IF `ch 9 -- the sureties answer for the debt` `the principal debtor is able to satisfy the debt` `the principal debtor has failed to pay the debt` EQUALS Obliged
    THEN PARTY `a surety`
         MUST `answer for the debt of the principal debtor`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `a surety` BECAUSE "ch 9: the surety did not answer for the debt after the principal debtor failed to pay it, having nothing wherewith to pay"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 9.4 and 9.5: the sureties' hold on the debtor's lands and rents, with the proviso.
-- src:25 | and let them have the lands and rents of the debtor, if they desire them, until they are indemnified for the debt which they have paid for him,
-- src:25 | unless the principal debtor can show proof that he is discharged thereof as against the said sureties.
@ref Chapter 9 clause 9.4-9.5 (src:25)
GIVEN `the surety has paid the debt for the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the surety desires the lands and rents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the surety has been indemnified for what he paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal debtor shows proof that he is discharged as against the surety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `ch 9 -- the surety may have the lands and rents of the debtor` IS
    IF `the surety has paid the debt for the debtor`
    THEN IF   `the surety desires the lands and rents`
          AND (NOT `the surety has been indemnified for what he paid`)
          AND (NOT `the principal debtor shows proof that he is discharged as against the surety`)
         THEN Entitled
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if they desire them", "until they are indemnified" and "unless the principal debtor can show proof that he is discharged".
         ELSE `Not entitled`
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: if, unless, until because these words qualify what a surety who has paid may have; the branch is reached by a surety who has not paid, who is outside the clause).
    ELSE `Entitlement not covered`

-- src:25 | and let them have the lands and rents of the debtor, if they desire them, until they are indemnified for the debt which they have paid for him,
-- src:25 | unless the principal debtor can show proof that he is discharged thereof as against the said sureties.
@ref Chapter 9 clause 9.4-9.5 (src:25)
GIVEN `the surety has paid the debt for the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the surety desires the lands and rents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the surety has been indemnified for what he paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal debtor shows proof that he is discharged as against the surety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 9 -- the sureties may have the lands and rents of the debtor until they are indemnified` IS
    IF `ch 9 -- the surety may have the lands and rents of the debtor` `the surety has paid the debt for the debtor` `the surety desires the lands and rents` `the surety has been indemnified for what he paid` `the principal debtor shows proof that he is discharged as against the surety` EQUALS Entitled
    THEN PARTY `a surety`
         MAY `have the lands and rents of the debtor until indemnified`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `Chapter 10 -- interest on a deceased borrower's debt to the Jews`

-- gloss (not the text's): "the Jews" is the text's name for the class of lenders; whether the
-- lender was one of them is taken as a plain fact.  The second limb is read as speaking of the same
-- debt as the first, "the debt" (fork F10).
-- src:27 | If one who has borrowed from the Jews any sum, great or small, die before that loan be repaid, the debt shall not bear interest while the heir is under age, of whomsoever he may hold;
@ref Chapter 10 clause 10.1 (src:27)
GIVEN `the loan was borrowed from the Jews` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the borrower died before the loan was repaid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the heir is under age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 10 -- the debt may bear interest` IS
    IF `the loan was borrowed from the Jews`
    THEN IF `the borrower died before the loan was repaid`
         THEN IF `the heir is under age`
              THEN Barred
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "while the heir is under age".
              ELSE `Not barred`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If one who has borrowed from the Jews any sum, great or small, die before that loan be repaid".
         ELSE `Not barred`
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: if, while because the "if" clause speaks of "one who has borrowed from the Jews", and the branch is reached by a loan from someone else).
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

-- src:27 | and if the debt fall into our hands, we will not take anything except the principal sum contained in the bond.
@ref Chapter 10 clause 10.2 (src:27)
GIVEN `the loan was borrowed from the Jews` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the borrower died before the loan was repaid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debt has fallen into the King's hands` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal sum contained in the bond` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum the King would take` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 10 -- the King may take this sum of the debt` IS
    IF   `the loan was borrowed from the Jews`
     AND `the borrower died before the loan was repaid`
    THEN IF `the debt has fallen into the King's hands`
         THEN IF `the sum the King would take` GREATER THAN `the principal sum contained in the bond`
              THEN Barred
              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "we will not take anything except the principal sum contained in the bond".
              ELSE `Not barred`
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and if the debt fall into our hands".
         ELSE `Not barred`
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: if, except because the "if" and the "except" govern a debt of 10.1 that has fallen into the King's hands, and the branch is reached by a loan that is not from the Jews or whose borrower has not died, which is the debt 10.1 speaks of (F10)).
    ELSE `Bar not covered`

-- src:27 | and if the debt fall into our hands, we will not take anything except the principal sum contained in the bond.
@ref Chapter 10 clause 10.2 (src:27)
GIVEN `the loan was borrowed from the Jews` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the borrower died before the loan was repaid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the debt has fallen into the King's hands` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
DECIDE `ch 10 -- the King will take nothing but the principal sum of a debt fallen into his hands` IS
    IF   `the loan was borrowed from the Jews`
     AND `the borrower died before the loan was repaid`
     AND `the debt has fallen into the King's hands`
    THEN PARTY `the King`
         SHANT `take from the debt anything except the principal sum contained in the bond`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the King` BECAUSE "ch 10: the King took more than the principal sum contained in the bond"
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `Chapter 11 -- the widow, the children and the residue`

-- 11.4 says "in like manner let it be done touching debts due to others than Jews": the three
-- rules below therefore take either kind of creditor (fork F11 on how far "in like manner" reaches).
-- The text names no one who must provide or pay in 11.1 to 11.3, so these are decision functions.
-- src:29 | And if anyone die indebted to the Jews, his wife shall have her dower and pay nothing of that debt;
-- src:29 | in like manner let it be done touching debts due to others than Jews.
@ref Chapter 11 clause 11.1 and 11.4 (src:29)
GIVEN `the husband died indebted to the Jews` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the husband died indebted to others than the Jews` IS A BOOLEAN
      `she is his wife` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `ch 11 -- the wife has her dower and pays nothing of the debt` IS
    IF   `she is his wife`
     AND (   `the husband died indebted to the Jews`
          OR `the husband died indebted to others than the Jews`)
    THEN Entitled
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: if because "if" states the situation the clause governs (a husband who died indebted); the branch is reached by a person who is not his wife or by a husband who owed nothing, of whom the text says nothing).
    ELSE `Entitlement not covered`

-- src:29 | and if any children of the deceased are left under age, necessaries shall be provided for them in keeping with the holding of the deceased;
-- src:29 | in like manner let it be done touching debts due to others than Jews.
@ref Chapter 11 clause 11.2 and 11.4 (src:29)
GIVEN `the deceased died indebted to the Jews` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased died indebted to others than the Jews` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a child of the deceased is left under age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `ch 11 -- necessaries shall be provided for the children under age, in keeping with the holding of the deceased` IS
    IF   `the deceased died indebted to the Jews`
      OR `the deceased died indebted to others than the Jews`
    THEN IF `a child of the deceased is left under age`
         THEN Entitled
         -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "and if any children of the deceased are left under age".
         ELSE `Not entitled`
    -- NOTHING-kind (word not the condition here: if, provided because the first "if" states the situation the clause governs, a debtor who died indebted, and "provided" is the verb in "necessaries shall be provided"; a deceased who owed nothing is outside what the clause decides).
    ELSE `Entitlement not covered`

-- gloss (not the text's): `the residue` is what is left of the deceased's estate after the
-- widow's dower and the necessaries for the children, a sum the person states.
-- src:29 | and out of the residue the debt shall be paid, reserving, however, service due to feudal lords;
-- src:29 | in like manner let it be done touching debts due to others than Jews.
@ref Chapter 11 clause 11.3 and 11.4 (src:29)
GIVEN `the debt` IS A NUMBER
      `the residue after the dower and the necessaries` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `ch 11 -- the amount of the debt paid out of the residue` IS
    IF `the debt` GREATER THAN `the residue after the dower and the necessaries`
    THEN `the residue after the dower and the necessaries`
    ELSE `the debt`

-- "reserving, however, service due to feudal lords": the payment of the debt does not reduce it.
-- src:29 | and out of the residue the debt shall be paid, reserving, however, service due to feudal lords;
@ref Chapter 11 clause 11.3 (src:29)
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `ch 11 -- the payment of the debt may be made at the expense of service due to feudal lords` IS Barred
